                <pb facs="0740" n="678" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg678"/>

                <p rendition="#center">(Sent from Reynosa April 30, 1878. Received at the city of
                    Mexico the same day at 10.58 p.m.)</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">Citizen Secretary of War:</p>
                <p>General R. Cuellar sent me the following yesterday from Matamoras:</p>
                <p>“I have learned from prisoners taken from the enemy that the total number of
                    enlisted men is from 160 to 200, who have crossed with all the leaders who were
                    in Texas.”</p>
                <closer><signed>S. CANALES.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
